/**
 * =====================================================================
 * FruitCropXL – Validation Framework (JUnit + CSV/YAML)
 * =====================================================================
 *
 * <h2>Overview</h2>
 * This mini-framework runs validation tests for FruitCropXL scenarios by:
 * <ol>
 *   <li>Loading <b>scenario.yaml</b> and <b>params.yaml</b> from a scenario folder.</li>
 *   <li>Running the model (via {@code ValidationTestBase.init()}) to produce
 *       <i>synthetic</i> CSV output.</li>
 *   <li>Reading <i>validation</i> CSV(s) specified in params.yaml.</li>
 *   <li>Comparing synthetic vs. validation series using:
 *       <ul>
 *         <li>Discrepancy tests (percentile mean difference)</li>
 *         <li>RMSE tests (root mean squared error)</li>
 *       </ul>
 *   </li>
 * </ol>
 *
 * <h2>Call Sequence (typical test)</h2>
 * <pre>
 *  JUnit @BeforeClass in a test class extending ValidationTestBase:
 *      validationDir = "dai-2012-12L";
 *      init();                           // 1) Build ValidationReader + run model
 *      readSyntheticOutput(...)          //    OR readSyntheticOutputsSameRows(...) for multi-CSV
 *
 *  inside init():
 *      validationReader = new ValidationReader(validationDir)
 *      scenario = validationReader.getScenario()
 *      applyScenarioSettings(scenario)
 *      mainInstance.resetGraph(); mainInstance.init(); derive(); runEnd(...)
 *      applyScenarioSettings(scenario)   // re-apply if init() overwrote flags
 *
 *  inside readSyntheticOutput(s):
 *      read synthetic CSV(s) -> syntheticDataList
 *      applyValidationSettings(params)   // wires discrepancyTestMethods / rmseTestMethods
 *
 *  JUnit @Test methods:
 *      discrepancyTestMethods.columnsWithinDiscrepancyThreshold(...)
 *      rmseTestMethods.hasLessOrEqualRMSE(...), optionally .at(steps)
 * </pre>
 *
 * <h2>Class Hierarchy & Roles</h2>
 * <pre>
 *  IValidationReader (interface)
 *      └─ ValidationReader
 *           - Reads YAML (params/scenario) and CSV(s)
 *           - Can merge multiple CSVs column-wise (same row count)
 *
 *  ValidationTestBase (abstract)
 *      - Owns ValidationReader, syntheticDataList, and test helpers (discrepancy/rmse)
 *      - Provides init(), readSyntheticOutput(s), and YAML -> runtime wiring
 *
 *  ValidationTestMethods (abstract)
 *      ├─ DiscrepancyTestMethods
 *      │    - Percentile mean-difference tests, with safe column matching
 *      └─ RMSETestMethods
 *           - RMSE tests, optional step filtering via .at(int...)
 *
 *  ValidationRunner
 *      - JUnit bootstrap (CLI), scenario selection, XML listener
 *
 *  Concrete JUnit classes (extend ValidationTestBase)
 *      - DefaultValidationUnitTest, StormValidationUnitTest, FOPSSatDryValidationUnitTest,
 *        Antony2010ValidationUnitTest, DAI2012With12LUnitTest, DAI2012With3LUnitTest
 * </pre>
 *
 * <h2>Data Flow</h2>
 * <pre>
 *  params.yaml
 *    discrepancy:
 *      dataset: [file1.csv, file2.csv]  # or single string
 *      threshold: 0.05
 *    rmse:
 *      dataset: file.csv                # or [file.csv, ...]
 *      synthetic-columns:
 *        - { name: ColumnA, rmse: 10.0 }
 *
 *  scenario.yaml
 *    file-name-model-options: ...
 *    max-steps: 1000
 *    use-shading-factor: true
 *    light-interception-mode: cpu
 * </pre>
 *
 * <h2>Java 1.5 Compatibility</h2>
 * <ul>
 *   <li>Raw types are used (e.g., {@code List} instead of {@code List&lt;T&gt;}).</li>
 *   <li>No diamond/generics syntax; no streams/lambdas.</li>
 *   <li>Use of {@code Double.valueOf(...)} when needed; avoid boxing constructors.</li>
 * </ul>
 *
 * <h2>Extending</h2>
 * <ol>
 *   <li>Add a new JUnit class extending {@code ValidationTestBase}.</li>
 *   <li>Set {@code validationDir} in {@code @BeforeClass}, call {@code init()},
 *       then {@code readSyntheticOutput(...)} or {@code readSyntheticOutputsSameRows(...)}.</li>
 *   <li>Add your assertions using {@code discrepancyTestMethods} and/or {@code rmseTestMethods}.</li>
 *   <li>Register the new class in {@link ValidationRunner#getTestScenarios()} if using the runner.</li>
 * </ol>
 */


